<title>BRAZIL: Brazil net dollar outflows at $99.9 mln April 14.</title>
<headline>Brazil net dollar outflows at $99.9 mln April 14.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preliminary figures for Brazil's commercial and financial foreign exchange contracts showed a $99.9 million deficit on April 14 in the commercial forex market, according to Central Bank data suplied to banks.</p>
<p>A banker with access to the figures said the Central Bank issued the following breakdown.</p>
<p>DOLLAR FLOWS ON APRIL 14</p>
<p>Exports: $198.9 million</p>
<p>Imports: $171.7 million</p>
<p>Finanancial buy: $212.9 million</p>
<p>Financial sell: $340 million</p>
<p>Net deficit: $99.9 million</p>
<p>APRIL DOLLAR FLOWS UP DATE</p>
<p>Exports: $2.043 billion</p>
<p>Imports: $2.023 billion</p>
<p>Financial buy: $2.800 billion</p>
<p>Financial sell: $2.539 billion</p>
<p>Net surplus: $281 million</p>
<p>Note: the figures were rounded off.</p>
<p>((--Alexandre Caverni, Sao Paulo newsroon, 55 11 2485418))</p>
</text>
